      "title": "Le matin",
      "description": "Talk about your morning routine with reflexive verbs.",
      "estimatedMinutes": 13,
      "sections": [
        {
          "type": "learn",
          "title": "Learn",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "heading": "Morning actions",
              "body": "Many morning actions are things you do to yourself: wake (yourself) up, wash (yourself), dress (yourself). French shows this with a small extra word: se réveiller (to wake up), se lever (to get up), se doucher (to shower), s'habiller (to get dressed).",
              "examples": [
                { "french": "Je me réveille à sept heures.", "english": "I wake up at seven o'clock." },
                { "french": "Je me lève.", "english": "I get up." },
                { "french": "Je me douche et je m'habille.", "english": "I shower and I get dressed." },
                { "french": "Je me lave dans la salle de bains.", "english": "I wash in the bathroom." },
                { "french": "Ensuite, je me coiffe.", "english": "Then, I do my hair." }
              ],
              "tip": "\"Le matin\" (in the morning) usually goes at the start or the end of the sentence: Le matin, je me lève tôt."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "vocabulary",
          "title": "Vocabulary",
          "items": [
