    {
      "id": "a1_u07_l02",
      "level": "A1",
      "unit": 7,
      "title": "Ma journée",
      "description": "Describe your day with common -er verbs in the present tense.",
      "estimatedMinutes": 12,
      "sections": [
        {
          "type": "learn",
          "title": "Learn",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "heading": "Talking about your day",
              "body": "Most French verbs end in -er: travailler (to work), manger (to eat), regarder (to watch), écouter (to listen to). With a few time words — le matin, à midi, l'après-midi — you can describe your whole day.",
              "examples": [
                { "french": "Le matin, je travaille.", "english": "In the morning, I work." },
                { "french": "À midi, je mange avec une collègue.", "english": "At noon, I eat with a colleague." },
                { "french": "L'après-midi, j'étudie le français.", "english": "In the afternoon, I study French." },
                { "french": "Je téléphone à ma mère le soir.", "english": "I phone my mother in the evening." },
                { "french": "Elle travaille dans un bureau.", "english": "She works in an office." }
              ],
              "tip": "\"Déjeuner\" is both a noun (le déjeuner, lunch) and a verb (déjeuner, to have lunch): Je déjeune à midi."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
