          "blocks": [
            {
              "heading": "Evening activities",
              "body": "In the evening — le soir — you have dinner (dîner), watch television, read a book (lire un livre) and finally go to bed (se coucher). \"Tard\" means late; its opposite is \"tôt\" (early).",
              "examples": [
                { "french": "Le soir, je dîne à huit heures.", "english": "In the evening, I have dinner at eight o'clock." },
                { "french": "Je regarde la télévision.", "english": "I watch television." },
                { "french": "Je me couche à dix heures.", "english": "I go to bed at ten o'clock." },
                { "french": "Après le dîner, je lis un livre.", "english": "After dinner, I read a book." },
                { "french": "Nous regardons un film.", "english": "We are watching a film." }
              ],
              "tip": "In France, dinner is often late — eight o'clock or even later is completely normal."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
